# Adopts the Recruitment Portal UAT Elastic Beanstalk environment. An import block only records "this existing AWS
# resource is managed by this address". It changes nothing in AWS.
#
# Left out on purpose:
#  - the Elastic Beanstalk application (shared with Production, so it lives in stacks/recruitment-portal/shared),
#  - the security group that Elastic Beanstalk generated for the old instance (it belongs to the environment's own
#    CloudFormation stack), the Elastic IP and the instance itself,
#  - the Auto Scaling group's registration with the target group Recruitment-UAT (added by hand; its group name is
#    generated by Elastic Beanstalk, so it is handled after this import, by reference).
#
# Workflow: terraform plan '-generate-config-out=generated.tf' (quote the argument in PowerShell), clean the draft
# into its own file, plan until the only differences are the intended ones, apply a saved plan.
# generated.tf is git-ignored on purpose and must never be committed.

import {
  to = aws_elastic_beanstalk_environment.uat
  id = "e-bpuguwpiki"
}
